1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
So much for that super-powerful spell of yours, Lineface.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:44,000
It seemed the Magic Knights had finally bested the Eye of the Midnight Sun's leader, until the Third Eye appeared, the Organization's three strongest members.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Oh man, looks like something didn't go as planned.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Do you know what we do to people who harm our friends?

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I detest anybody who hurts Licht. I hate them.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Raya the Disloyal, Thedo the Despair, and Fauna the Hateful.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
I know you'll succeed where I failed. Thank you, my friends.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The Black Bulls swiftly found themselves outmatched.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Now, let's get this over with.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Ha!

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Spirit magic, salamander's breath.

15
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:24,000
But then, the captain of the green praying mantises, Jack the Ripper, Blue Rose Knight's captain, Charlotte Roselay, and Silver Eagle's captain, Nozel Silva, arrived, turning the tide of battle once again.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
You're having way too much fun on your own here, Yami! You should let the rest of us in on it!

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Today, time on!

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:02:04,980
Thank you.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:34,980
Thank you.

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:03:04,980
Thank you.

21
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:10,460
And then, that woman turned Baro into a giant living mass of mud.

22
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:16,740
I see. It sounds to me like the Eye of the Midnight Sun was using you and your brother for their own purposes.

23
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:29,400
I guess. But we were still the ones who abducted all of those children. We were the ones who stole their magic. And so now, I'm going to take responsibility for my actions as well as my brothers.

24
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:33,140
I'll turn myself into the magic knights.

25
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:38,820
That's right. Earlier, back in the cave, Asta said something.

26
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:46,900
Good. And once you get that out of the way, you and I should be friends. With all the cool magic you can do, I bet you're going to be a pretty popular guy.

27
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:51,020
We'll be friends. I'm truly sorry.

28
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:57,700
There's hardly any point apologizing to me. Once you're done paying your dues, you're going to be Asta's friend, right?

29
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:03,000
So if I were you, I would start praying for your new buddy to win his fight and get back here in one piece.

30
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,040
Honestly, Asta, what are you doing out there? Finish it up already.

31
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,380
Asta, please stay safe.

32
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:21,560
I mean, not that it matters to me what happens to that insect, because it totally doesn't. Not in the slightest.

33
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:26,460
Why does this keep happening? And who am I even talking to?

34
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:31,560
She likes Asta too? Is that the someone special he's got his heart set on?

35
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,340
There's no way he'd notice me with someone like her around.

36
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:43,420
No. This isn't the time to be thinking about that. I should be getting things ready here for when they get back.

37
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,240
Everything else can wait. Right.

38
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,500
Ooh, second course. Yum.

39
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:57,840
Shame on you, getting greedy. It's not polite to hog all the interesting battles for yourself, you know.

40
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,360
I've got to wonder, how's it going to feel to tear them apart?

41
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:05,480
Probably not very satisfying. Kind of like ripping up a sheet of paper.

42
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:09,380
I was just about to finish him off when you morons decide to show up.

43
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:15,060
Keh, keh, keh. Yeah, I'm sure you were. Looking more ragged than usual over there.

44
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,120
Pfft. Me? Please.

45
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,580
Keh, keh, keh.

46
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:24,040
How about I work out some of my anger issues by cutting you into tiny pieces?

47
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,320
And there it is. You're nuts.

48
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,320
My sincerest apologies. Forgive me.

49
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:33,460
Keh, keh, keh. Scared now? I wasn't really going to do it.

50
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:37,840
I'd much rather wait until you're back in fighting shape before our next little skirmish.

51
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:40,120
There isn't any point if it's not a challenge.

52
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:42,880
Must we always come to get you out of trouble?

53
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,940
You can't even stand up, you miserable man.

54
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:51,060
Hey, it's not like that. The ground just loves my ass so much it doesn't ever want to let me go.

55
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,440
Don't be an idiot.

56
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:56,420
The Earth has no love for an unwashed miscreate like yourself.

57
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,500
Ooh, burn.

58
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,320
That's some mouth you got on you.

59
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,680
Not going to be easy to find yourself a husband, huh?

60
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:05,140
Now she's angry.

61
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:09,180
I don't need any man to marry me. The battlefield is my partner.

62
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:13,780
I get that you're a warrior woman and all, but even for you, that's pretty sad.

63
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,960
Does he have no regard for my feelings?

64
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:23,860
Why? Why did I have to fall for him? It's like some kind of cruel joke.

65
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:27,520
But as hard as I try, I can't keep him out of my head.

66
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,380
Well, I certainly can't tell him anything now.

67
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:35,340
But if I did tell him someday, what would my squad think?

68
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:37,440
You've got to be kidding me, Char!

69
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,380
You know he's a man, right? A gross man!

70
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,480
What am I doing?

71
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:44,980
Now isn't the time for this.

72
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:49,540
So, the Eye of the Midnight Sun, its leader and his top brass.

73
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,900
The highest ranking members of the organization that attacked our kingdom.

74
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:56,200
I won't waste this chance.

75
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,500
I'll bury you with my own hands.

76
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,820
Ooh, Nozel, you are so cool.

77
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:03,640
You just sit there and try to stay out of trouble, foreigner.

78
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:08,380
Your concern for my well-being is truly touching, oh great and mighty captain.

79
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:12,980
Hey, how do you guys think he gets his hair to do that braid thing?

80
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:16,740
He's royal, so I figure he has a servant take care of it for him, don't you think?

81
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,380
Honestly, I wouldn't be surprised if he had his own personal hairstylist.

82
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:23,520
I think that would qualify as the worst job ever.

83
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,060
What? You think he takes the time to braid his own things?

84
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,660
Oh yeah, he probably has lots of time on his hands. Loser.

85
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:34,260
No, on second thought, perhaps I ought to bury you before those other four.

86
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:37,120
You don't want to waste your magic on some foreigner.

87
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,440
Show no mercy.

88
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,160
Kick hit.

89
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:48,940
Oh yeah, let's do this, guys! I'm totally ready to go! We'll take these jerks down, no problem!

90
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:51,200
You won't be joining this fight.

91
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:51,500
Huh?

92
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:58,100
The captains have taken to the battlefield. Anybody who interferes now will only get in our way.

93
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:01,160
Especially a pathetic, magicless commoner like you.

94
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:07,740
Excellent. What better place to find true despair than at the end of an endless battle?

95
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:12,540
And no despair is more delicious than that of the mighty when they face certain death.

96
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:14,200
What the hell's he talking about?

97
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:17,060
Looks like we've got some rat-catching to do.

98
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:22,380
Jeez, Vero is way too excited about this fight. Sounds boring to me.

99
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:29,820
Well, whatever. I guess I can put forth some effort for Licht's sake.

100
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:35,140
And by the way, I'm calling dibs on this beautiful young lady.

101
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:38,380
When I win, you and I are going out for a drink, gorgeous.

102
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:43,020
When you win? I'm afraid we're never going to be clinking glasses then.

103
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:46,860
Briar creation magic! Corpse hunting briar tree!

104
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,440
Oh!

105
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,860
Suffering magic! Death!

106
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:10,020
Someone's eager for a fight. You're mine, Beastie.

107
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,720
Well, well. The praying mantis squad.

108
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:16,360
Then I'll just squash you like the insignificant bugs that you are.

109
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:19,280
You think so? Well, we'll see!

110
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:22,720
You're confident for a bug? Fine!

111
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,900
Let's see you smile while I'm ripping you limp from leg!

112
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,920
Go back home!

113
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:31,120
I've been waiting for this. Finally.

114
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,800
Mercury magic! Silver spears!

115
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:42,760
Yet another foolish person attempting to harm Licht.

116
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,660
For that, you'll die.

117
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:50,940
Looks like the salamander girl's flames are melting your mercury.

118
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:53,180
You want to swap opponent, silver boy?

119
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:57,440
I don't think so. Those flames are hardly enough to best me.

120
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:01,120
You have no idea what I had to do to get where I am.

121
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:05,400
You're the also who haste tree.

122
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,340
Good luck!

123
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:07,960
Bloody guts!

124
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:08,760
Run now!

125
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:22,640
It shithcl

126
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:37,000
All this magic flying around, it looks like some kind of natural disaster.

127
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,040
I can't see through all this dust.

128
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,620
Jeez, they're really fighting hard.

129
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:46,760
Better be careful, Jack. You talk a good game, but you cut it kind of close.

130
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,660
Looks like Charlotte's doing well, though.

131
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:52,220
And those L's bangs haven't budged at all.

132
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:53,380
You can see?

133
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:56,960
Remember, Ki? I can sense them.

134
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:57,480
Yeah.

135
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,480
Venral, you ready?

136
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,280
For what, sir?

137
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:06,060
You've been resting up for a while now. You ought to have enough mana for a spatial spell.

138
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:10,800
You mean we're leaving? Sure, I'm ready. Let the other captains handle this. We can just...

139
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:19,260
The Magic Knight captains are as powerful as I expected them to be.

140
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,380
However, they are no match for the Third Eye.

141
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:30,040
Our people are much loved by the mana of this world, and that is why there must be some mistake.

142
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:38,940
How could an ordinary human, one who's magicless, clearly shunned by the mana, possess that grimoire?

143
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:42,000
I must retrieve it from his unworthy hands at once.

144
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:46,940
He's been weakened, but I'm not gonna risk letting him get away.

145
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:50,820
Ah, yes. I expected this from you.

146
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:53,000
He's countering?

147
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,720
Not good. Look out, sir!

148
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:55,880
Oh, dear.

149
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:58,340
You misjudged our boss, I see.

150
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,000
I'll end you this time.

151
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,240
Finishingly.

152
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:07,900
You're going after the boss, too, aren't you?

153
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,940
All right. Bring it!

154
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,940
How did he get over there?

155
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,520
It shouldn't have been possible in all this confusion.

156
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,840
That's the kind of thing you can do when you learn to read key.

157
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,720
No one noticed.

158
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:24,840
No one.

159
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:27,120
None of us could sense this boy.

160
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:28,960
Because he has no magic.

161
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,520
We're gonna get you this time!

162
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:35,560
Thanks for trusting that I was gonna take one last shot at you while I had the chance.

163
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:39,040
As for me, I put my trust in our magicless freak here.

164
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,840
My magic is never giving up!

165
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:59,160
Gotcha!

166
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:02,600
So what'd you think about my magic-free smash attack?

167
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,740
You trying to take all the credit, kid?

168
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:07,300
Sorry, Captain.

169
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,720
Not bad. You really pushed past your limits that time.

170
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:11,680
Thank you!

171
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:16,700
Where's Lyft?

172
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,580
Oh, no!

173
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,020
Eyes forward, PC!

174
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,420
That little runt!

175
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,960
He left us to the dust!

176
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:24,520
Kid!

177
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:24,860
Kid!

178
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,900
So much for getting all the glory!

179
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,220
We're magic knight captains!

180
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:31,320
We can't fall behind!

181
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,500
It's up to us to take care of the rest!

182
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,440
Captain Yami?

183
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,780
Wonder if any more of their friends are gonna show up.

184
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:38,920
I guess we'll see.

185
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:39,860
It would be so cool!

186
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:41,420
Now's your chance to finish him

187
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,740
while the other captains keep the rest of them busy!

188
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,420
Hmm.

189
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:51,300
He's glowing!

190
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,000
What the...

191
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,200
No!

192
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:57,380
When that brat hit licked with his anti-magic attack,

193
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:00,380
it broke the spell of sealing that was cast on him!

194
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:02,320
That's not good.

195
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:06,100
That power had been set aside for a day still to come.

196
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:11,100
This cannot be!

197
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,340
Why do you have that grimoire?

198
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,600
Why do you wield them?

199
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,980
The Demon Slayer Sword

200
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:21,160
and the Demon Dweller Sword?

201
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,200
What's he saying?

202
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:27,480
Those swords belong to the Master!

203
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,480
The Master...

204
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:30,480
The Master...

205
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,460
According to our intel,

206
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:35,340
the Master is the leader of the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

207
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:39,220
Does this mean he isn't the Master?

208
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:41,820
You keep saying this crap!

209
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,120
Well, I'm sick of it!

210
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,780
It doesn't matter who this Master guy is, okay?

211
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:48,820
This grimoire and these swords are mine!

212
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,680
I don't care if they're all beat up!

213
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:52,820
Now quit with all the accusations!

214
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:55,200
They're not yours!

215
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:56,800
Give them back!

216
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:00,980
That grimoire could never belong to you!

217
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:06,220
The Master's grimoire could never be yours, filthy human!

218
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:09,620
Oh boy!

219
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:10,840
What now, Captain?

220
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:13,220
Things aren't looking so good, huh?

221
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,800
Well, this should be fun!

222
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,560
Damn, no!

223
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:20,540
No way!

224
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:23,120
It absorbed my separating magic like it was nothing!

225
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,900
That's an enormous mass of pure magic power!

226
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:28,320
If he releases it, we're all dead!

227
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:30,900
It'll destroy everything in the surrounding area!

228
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,540
But what do we do?

229
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,520
Even we cannot stop this!

230
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:37,220
How much mana is he channeling?

231
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,580
He's been holding back!

232
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:41,260
He could have obliterated us anytime he wanted to!

233
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:46,060
I should have never come on this stupid mission!

234
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,340
Actually, scratch that!

235
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:50,440
I should never have joined this squad to begin with!

236
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,980
Stop running your mouth!

237
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,380
Nobody wants to hear it!

238
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:55,740
Besides, this could be our chance!

239
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,620
Just think of all the limits we could push past!

240
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,880
We'll be up against some real power!

241
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,600
Let's go!

242
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:04,100
No way!

243
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:05,040
Seriously!

244
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:07,040
Have you people gone crazy here?

245
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:07,600
Hey!

246
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:10,360
Shut up and pull it together, Fen'Roll!

247
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,720
